=== layout: one-panel

# Southern White and Black Rhinos Differ at Eight Positions

@body

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/south_black.drawn.svg)

Eight positions differ. The completed matrix is symmetric.

{table-style=comparison border="0.5pt solid #C5CBD2" table-group=rhino-three padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
|  | N.Wh. | S.Wh. | Blk.R |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| N.Wh. | 0 | 4 | 12 |
| S.Wh. | 4 | 0 | 8 |
| Blk.R | 12 | 8 | 0 |


=== layout: subsection

# Three Rhinos: Build the Tree

=== layout: two-panels

# Step 1: Find the Smallest Distance

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-three padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
|  | N.Wh. | S.Wh. | Blk.R |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| N.Wh. |  |  |  |
| S.Wh. | 4 |  |  |
| Blk.R | 12 | 8 |  |

Read the lower half. Which pair joins first?

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_0.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Step 2: Join the White Rhinos

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-three padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
|  | N.Wh. | S.Wh. | Blk.R |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| N.Wh. |  |  |  |
| S.Wh. | [4]{background-color=#FFF1B8 border="0.5pt solid #222222"} |  |  |
| Blk.R | 12 | 8 |  |

Distance 4 gives node height 4 / 2 = 2. Each tip branch has length 2.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_1.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Step 3: Update the Cluster Distance

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-three padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
|  | N.Wh. | S.Wh. | Blk.R |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| N.Wh. |  |  |  |
| S.Wh. | 4 |  |  |
| Blk.R | 12 | 8 |  |

What is the distance from the white-rhino cluster to Blk.R.?

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_1.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Average 12 and 8 to Get 10

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-two padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
| | White | Blk.R |
| --- | --- | --- |
| White | | |
| Blk.R | 10 | |

White = N.Wh. and S.Wh.

(12 + 8) / 2 = 10. Each original sequence gets equal weight.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_1.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Step 4: Join the Final Clusters

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-two padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
| | White | Blk.R |
| --- | --- | --- |
| White | | |
| Blk.R | 10 | |

The root height is 10 / 2 = 5.

The white-rhino branch is 5 - 2 = 3; the black-rhino branch is 5 - 0 = 5.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_2.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# The Three-Rhino Tree Is Complete

@left

- Each white-rhino tip branch has length 2.
- The white-rhino cluster joins the root with a branch of length 3.
- The black-rhino branch has length 5.
- Every root-to-tip path has length 5.
- The fitted white-to-black path is 10; the original inputs were 12 and 8.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_2.drawn.svg)

